  "mn12:8.11": "<i>Mahaggataṁ.</i> This term is used, together with “immeasurable / unlimited,” in the standard description of the awareness generated in the practice of the brahmavihāras (<a href='https://suttacentral.net/sn42.8'>SN 42:8</a>). According to Ven. Anuruddha in MN 127, however, an enlarged mind is not immeasurable. Its range of awareness is larger than the body but still measurable, ranging in distance from the shade of a tree to the earth bounded by the ocean.",
  "mn12:8.12": "",
  "mn12:8.13": "",
  "mn12:8.14": "",
  "mn12:8.15": "",
  "mn12:8.16": "",
  "mn12:8.17": "On the various levels of release, see <a href='https://suttacentral.net/dn15'>DN 15</a>, <a href='https://suttacentral.net/mn43'>MN 43</a>, and <a href='https://suttacentral.net/an9.43'>AN 9:43–45</a>.",
  "mn12:8.18": "",
